# Deployment workflow

Vercel is production hosting. It is **not** the compiler, linter, test runner, or `next build`. Failed production builds still bill **Build CPU** (Kitletics turbo, often 4–12 min). Agent loops that push “to see if Vercel builds” caused 16 Kitletics production deploys in ~6 days.

Until the user says **Deploy this now.**: do not `git push`, do not deploy, do not create commits merely to trigger a Vercel build.

## Required

```text
PLAN
→ IMPLEMENT LOCALLY
→ LINT
→ TYPECHECK
→ TEST
→ PRODUCTION BUILD
→ COST CHECK
→ REVIEW DIFF
→ COMMIT
→ PUSH
```

```bash
npm run validate:local          # lint, typecheck, test, next build
npm run audit:vercel-cost       # cost anti-patterns — do not “fix” by deploying
```

Fix lint / type / test / build failures **locally**. Batch related application changes into **one** deployment candidate. Docs, reports, `.cursor/`, and other non-app files must not rebuild production (`vercel.json` `ignoreCommand` → `node scripts/vercel-ignored-build.mjs`; exit 0 = skip, exit 1 = build).

## Forbidden

```text
CHANGE → PUSH → WAIT FOR VERCEL → FIX → PUSH
```

Do not use Vercel to discover TypeScript, lint, test, or `next build` errors. Do not auto-push or auto-deploy.

## Mandatory completion output (implementation tasks)

```text
LOCAL VALIDATION:
Lint:
Types:
Tests:
Production build:

VERCEL COST IMPACT
Build CPU: LOWER / NEUTRAL / HIGHER
Fluid CPU: LOWER / NEUTRAL / HIGHER
Origin Transfer: LOWER / NEUTRAL / HIGHER
ISR: LOWER / NEUTRAL / HIGHER
Images: LOWER / NEUTRAL / HIGHER
Observability: LOWER / NEUTRAL / HIGHER

DEPLOYMENT REQUIRED: YES/NO
SAFE TO DEPLOY: YES/NO
```

Any **HIGHER** cost line must be explained. `SAFE TO DEPLOY: YES` only after lint, typecheck, tests, and production build passed locally. Push/deploy only when the user says **Deploy this now.**
